{"hit_id": "MM-58210", "pi_name": "Elena Rodriguez", "date": "2025-04-10", "source": "STAT News op-ed", "excerpt": "Dr. Elena Rodriguez of Dana-Farber writes that the NIH\u2019s sudden termination of grants studying single-cell resistance in triple-negative breast cancer \u2018is not just a bureaucratic decision \u2014 it is a death sentence for patients who have no other options.\u2019 She argues that cutting genomic research during an active funding freeze is akin to abandoning the front line of oncology.", "tone": "sharp criticism, accusatory"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58211", "pi_name": "Marcus Whitfield", "date": "2025-06-22", "source": "Senate HELP testimony", "excerpt": "Testifying before the Senate Health Committee, Dr. Whitfield of Johns Hopkins warned that the administration\u2019s elimination of diversity-focused Alzheimer\u2019s biomarker studies \u2018will set back early detection in Black and Hispanic communities by a decade or more.\u2019 He called the cuts \u2018a form of health care discrimination through policy.\u2019", "tone": "sharp criticism, urgent"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58212", "pi_name": "Anika Sharma", "date": "2025-09-05", "source": "X/Twitter", "excerpt": "Dr. Anika Sharma at Cleveland Clinic: \u2018My deep learning MRI work on myocardial fibrosis just got defunded because it used an algorithm labeled \u201cDEI\u2010adjacent.\u201d This is not efficiency\u2014it's ideology over patients. I\u2019ll be joining the #StandUpForScience rally in D.C. next week.\u2019", "tone": "sharp criticism, activist"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58213", "pi_name": "Sofia Marquez", "date": "2025-07-14", "source": "university town hall", "excerpt": "At a WashU town hall, Dr. Marquez said that HHS\u2019s new restrictions on international collaborations have halted her lab\u2019s work on carbapenem-resistant Klebsiella. \u2018I have postdocs whose visas were flagged for \u201csensitive research\u201d on a bacteria that kills 50,000 Americans a year. This is bureaucracy weaponized against public health.\u2019", "tone": "sharp criticism, frustrated"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58214", "pi_name": "Latoya Jackson", "date": "2026-01-20", "source": "local TV interview", "excerpt": "Dr. Latoya Jackson, speaking on North Carolina public TV, said that Trump\u2019s freeze on community-based hypertension research in rural Black communities \u2018is hurting the very people who trusted us. We can\u2019t hold blood pressure screenings if our funding is cut for not being \u201cpatriotic enough.\u201d\u2019", "tone": "mild criticism, patient-centered"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58215", "pi_name": "Carlos Alberto Gomez", "date": "2026-03-11", "source": "Bluesky", "excerpt": "Dr. Gomez at UTHSCSA posted: \u2018ICE agents showing up at community health centers on the border? That\u2019s the real toxin driving preterm birth\u2014not my research. The administration is using immigration enforcement to terrorize pregnant women into silence.\u2019", "tone": "sharp criticism, angry"}
