ism and cardiovascular health isn't just bad policy\u2014it's a direct attack on the lives of Black communities. My patients deserve better than this administration's willful ignorance.", "tone": "Sharp, critical"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58221", "pi_name": "Adebayo O. Adeyemi", "date": "2025-05-22", "source": "STAT News op-ed", "excerpt": "By slashing funding for research on redlining and clinical trial participation, we're not just losing data\u2014we're entrenching cancer disparities that will kill Black women for decades. This is an act of public health sabotage.", "tone": "Sharp, accusatory"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58222", "pi_name": "Sofia M. Reyes", "date": "2025-03-14", "source": "Senate HELP testimony", "excerpt": "The administration's cancellation of community-based nutrition interventions directly harms pregnant people in food deserts. It will increase preterm births and widen disparities, plain and simple.", "tone": "Mild criticism, factual"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58223", "pi_name": "Ethan J. Park", "date": "2025-09-10", "source": "Bluesky", "excerpt": "When you criminalize LGBTQ+ youth and cut substance use funding, you're not protecting anyone\u2014you're pushing kids into worse outcomes. This is a moral failure, not a budget choice.", "tone": "Sharp, moralistic"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58224", "pi_name": "Mei-Ling Chen", "date": "2025-08-27", "source": "University press release", "excerpt": "Our multi-cohort study shows that wildfire smoke from climate change increases preterm birth risk by 15%. These findings underscore the urgent need for climate adaptation in maternal health.", "tone": "Neutral, scientific"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58225", "pi_name": "Rebecca S. Thompson", "date": "2025-06-15", "source": "Local TV interview", "excerpt": "The PEARL trial is testing a more precise thrombolytic approach for intermediate-risk PE. Early data suggest we can reduce bleeding complications while maintaining efficacy.", "tone": "Neutral, optimistic"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58226", "pi_name": "Aisha Okafor", "date": "2025-07-19", "source": "Open letter", "excerpt": "Deporting community health workers in rural Texas is tearing apart the very network that prevents maternal deaths among Black women. This administration's immigration policy is a death sentence for my patients.", "tone": "Sharp, urgent"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58227", "pi_name": "Luis Miguel Castro", "date": "2025-10-02", "source": "University town hall", "excerpt": "Cutting EPA monitoring and NIH funding for agricultural worker health is unconscionable\u2014these workers face particulate exposures that damage their hearts, and we're turning our backs on them.", "tone": "Mildly critical, concerned"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58228", "pi_name": "Koji Tanaka", "date": "2025-11-08", "source": "X/Twitter", "excerpt": "Our latest findings on broadly neutralizing antibodies targeting the hemagglutinin stem could lead to a universal flu vaccine. Proud of the team's progress, but we need stable federal funding to continue.", "tone": "Neutral, hopeful"}

